## Intent & Decisions
The user wanted to move the left arrow 'send session to agents' shortcut to another key. The docs (code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-view) say that key cannot be rebound; only the leftArrowOpensAgents setting in /config turns it off. The user chose to turn it off in the repo setup, apply it locally, and use /bg instead.

## Actions & Verification
- Backed up ~/.claude.json to the job tmp dir, ran merge_json on a copy: jq -S diff showed only the added "leftArrowOpensAgents": false.
- Applied merge_json to the real ~/.claude.json; jq shows false. A second run left the mtime unchanged (idempotent).
- Ran merge_json with claude_settings.json on a copy of ~/.claude/settings.json: output identical to the input, so the refactor kept the settings merge behavior.
- Did not run full setup_claude from the worktree, because it would symlink ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md to the worktree AGENTS.md.

## Errors & Mistakes
None

## Attempts & Outcomes
Considered adding the key to claude_settings.json like remoteControlAtStartup. Rejected after reading the 2.1.280 binary (see Findings).

## Findings & Constraints
In Claude Code 2.1.280, global config keys are listed in an array that includes leftArrowOpensAgents. Only keys in a second list (ube: theme, editorMode, remoteControlAtStartup, teammateMode, notification flags, and a few others) are read from settings.json. leftArrowOpensAgents is not in that list, so it must live in ~/.claude.json. ~/.claude.json is also written by running Claude Code sessions; the jq merge rewrites it only when the key is missing or different.

## Open Questions
A future Claude Code release may move leftArrowOpensAgents into settings.json; if so, move it into claude_settings.json and delete claude_global_config.json.
